<p>
  This policy explains which personal data is processed when you use the AI-Notepad subscription edition (the Mac app and
  the subscription server) and this website, why, who it is shared with, how long it is kept and how to use your rights.
  In short: <strong>your meeting audio is processed to be transcribed and is not stored on our servers; your notes,
  transcripts and recordings stay on your devices.</strong>
</p>

<h2>1. Controller</h2>
<p>
  {operatorName}, {operatorBusinessId}, {operatorAddress}. For any privacy question or request: {contactEmail}. The EU
  General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and Finnish data protection law apply.
</p>

<h2>2. Scope</h2>
<p>
  This policy covers the subscription edition. If you use the open-source developer edition with your own API keys, your
  data never reaches our server; it goes directly to the providers you chose and is subject to their terms.
</p>

<h2>3. How meeting content flows</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The <strong>live transcript</strong> is produced on your Mac by an on-device speech model; the audio doesn't leave your device for it.</li>
  <li>
    <strong>Final transcript and speaker separation:</strong> when the meeting ends, the recording is passed through our
    server to ElevenLabs. Our server does not write the audio to disk or keep it; it only adds the duration to your usage.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Notes, live translation, “What did I miss?” and Ask:</strong> the relevant parts of the transcript are passed
    through our server to Anthropic's Claude model and the answer returns to your device. Our server does not store or log
    this text; it only counts the tokens used.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Your notes, transcripts and recordings</strong> are stored on your Mac and iPhone and, if you turned on iCloud
    sync, in your own iCloud account. We cannot access them.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Integrations</strong> (Notion, Slack, Microsoft Teams, Discord, Zoom, Linear, Jira): content is sent at your
    request directly from your device to that service; it does not pass through our server.
  </li>
</ul>
<p>
  Before recording, it is your responsibility to inform participants and, where required, obtain their consent. You decide
  about the meeting content, including what participants say; we process it only on your behalf to provide the service.
</p>

