</p>

<h2>7. Retention</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Account, device registrations, meeting session records and monthly usage: while your account exists; deleted immediately when you delete your account.</li>
  <li>Sign-in links: valid for 15 minutes; deleted by the next day once used or expired.</li>
  <li>Refresh tokens: deleted by the next day once expired or signed out.</li>
  <li>Daily usage: 2 days. IP-hashed trial record: that day only.</li>
  <li>Processed Stripe events and total daily spend (not personal): 90 days.</li>
  <li>Technical logs: for Cloudflare's log retention period. [Verify: period]</li>
  <li>Database restore points (Cloudflare D1 Time Travel): up to 30 days.</li>
  <li>Invoices and payment records: at Stripe for the period required by Finnish accounting law.</li>
</ul>

<h2>8. Deleting your account</h2>
<p>
  You can delete your account at any time with “Delete account” on the <a href={pagePath("account", "en")}>account page</a>.
  Any unfinished subscription is first cancelled immediately at Stripe; then your account, sessions, sign-in links, device
  registrations, meeting session records, usage, subscription record and Stripe customer mapping are deleted in a single
  transaction. What remains: today's trial counter (per IP hash, not linked to the account, deleted at the end of the day),
  invoices at Stripe (legal obligation) and technical logs until they expire. Notes and recordings on your devices stay
  where they are; you delete them in the app.
</p>

<h2>9. Your rights</h2>
<p>
  You have the right to access, rectify and erase your data, to restrict processing, to data portability and to object to
  processing based on legitimate interest. Send your request to {contactEmail}; we reply within one month. You can lodge a
  complaint with the Finnish Data Protection Ombudsman (Tietosuojavaltuutetun toimisto, tietosuoja.fi) or the supervisory
  authority in your country.
</p>

<h2>10. Security</h2>
<p>
  All connections are encrypted (TLS). Tokens are stored on the server only as one-way hashes, IP addresses as keyed hashes,
  and app requests are verified with App Attest. Our API keys exist only as secrets on the server.
</p>

<h2>11. Children</h2>
<p>The service is not intended for anyone under 18.</p>

<h2>12. Changes</h2>
<p>
  If we change this policy we update its date, and we announce material changes in the app or by email before they take
  effect.
</p>
